nodecode-anki is a rewrite of suhas-svg's suhas-svg/hermes_anki:

  https://github.com/suhas-svg/hermes_anki
  commit bc89df834fb104b8d69c6444f35a5ae6b3764dd7

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 suhas-svg (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the whole plugin. The original is a Python Hermes Agent
plugin: an AnkiConnect client on the standard library, five model tools
(anki_decks, anki_add_cards, anki_search, anki_due, anki_answer), a /anki
slash command, a `hermes anki` CLI command and a study skill. This cell is
Common Lisp: the same five tools and the same /anki command, the same
AnkiConnect actions with the same arguments and the same search queries,
the same JSON answers a model reads, and the same HTML-to-plain-text
rendering of a card's question and answer. The config keys carry over
(anki_url, default_deck, default_model, request_timeout, max_cards, plus the
optional API key, read here from api_key or the variable api_key_env names
instead of only from the environment). Requests go through the image's own
HTTP call; nothing is fetched at run time and there is no Python.

What was left out: the `hermes anki` CLI subcommand, which a harness shape
does not carry (the same status, decks and search are the tools, the /anki
command and the help topic), and the bundled study skill, whose card-writing
and quiz rules now live in the cell's own primer and help text. The tests
against a fake AnkiConnect server are replaced by this cell's own test
system, which stubs HTTP and asserts the same protocol.
